      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1905-11-04_WidnesExaminer_art0029" n="art0029">
        <head>WARRINGTON RURAL DISTRICT</head>
        <p>WARRINGTON RURAL DISTRICT</p>
        <p>COUNCIL.</p>
        <p>The Alleged Nuisance at Penketh.</p>
        <p>The monthly meeting of the Warrington Rural Dis- trict Council was held at Bewsey Chambers on Wednes- day when there were present—Mr. Brooks (in the chair), Dr. Murray,Messrs.Forshaw,Houghton,Knowles, Thompson, Longton, Backhouse,. Mather, J. C. Sutton (clerk), S. Sutton (assistant clerk), H. H. Burnage (assistant surveyor), F. W. Kerfoot (inspector), and Dr. Sephton (medical officer.)</p>
        <p>THE ALLEGED NUISANCE AT PENKETH. The CLERK reported that he bad received a letter from Fleetwood Chemical Company in which they stated that they were in. negotiation for another site for their works and hoped in the course of the next fortnight to have made terms with the local authorities. Perhaps he (the clerk) would be good enough to assure the Council that they were doing their utmost to remove the present works and that there would be very little delay as soon as they got the agreement through Mr. KEFtFOOT reported that the work was still being carried on, but there had been no further complaints for the reason that the wind had been blowing away from Penketh. On Monday last he was in Penketh, and the stench from the works was very bad. He had consulted with the Clerk, and they had decided to take legal pro- ceedings. The case would be heard at the Warrington Potty Sessions on the 15th inst, when Mr. Browne would prosecute on behalf of the Council. Dr. AIURRAX : Probably the reason why there hag been no complaints is that the people are under the impression that the company are gaining. The Inspector's report was adopted.</p>
      </div>
