      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1905-11-04_WidnesExaminer_art0062" n="art0062">
        <head>WARRINGTON PHOTOGRAPHIC SOCIETY.</head>
        <p>THE WARRINGTON PHOTOGRAPHIC SOCIETY.</p>
        <p>Members' Successes.</p>
        <p>Mr. James V. Moore is to be congratulated on his success in winning the first prize of £lO in the Warwick open competion for a very fine picture of the organ screen, Chester Cathedral, a copy of which may be seen in the window of Mr. Harold Smith, Bridge street. The photograph is a " straight" and direct print from a" Rainbow" 12 xlO plate and quite deserves the encomioums passed upon it. The society shares in his success to the extent of £5, The Warwick Dry Plate Company giving a donation of this amount to the Club of which the winner is a member. Other members who have scored in various" open " competitions in the last two or three months have been Mr. F. Eardley who was awarded a medal for a picture entitled " His only steed " ; Mr. John W. Mills gains a medal for a very pretty sea and cloud study ; Mr. Kenneth F. Bishop for a set of slides entitled" Stories without words " is awarded a plaque and a camera ; Mrs. A. C. Smithson, medal for a character study called "Daddy," whilst Mr. Henry Bond—a former president—represented the Society at the Ex- hibition which closed last week of the Royal Photographic Society in London, his pictures" Return- ing to the Fold" ond " Deserted Ice" being selected by the committee along with about 400 others out of some 2,500 pictures sent up. The first picture gains a further distinction for the photographer, as it was pur- chased at the Exhibition. The Society is to be cordially congratulated on the general advance in its work which . manifested by these successes. Is 41. Index to Inside Pages.</p>
        <p>PAGE. 2. Women's Chat and Fashions. St. Peter's Sale of Work. Rural Council meetings. 3. Our Local Churches. Football. Board of Guardians. " The W hite Rose " (serial). 6. Elections : The Non-Traders' meetings. Town Council Business. Ambulance Competition. "Love in Whitechapel,"by Halliwell Sutcliffe. 7. Children's Corner. " Travel Extraordinary," by Eustace Reynolds</p>
