        <p>To add to Warrington's misfortunes, Elliot Harris has come once more under the ban of the Union, and is now doing time 'to the extent of one week. I under- stand that he ventured • to express his views rather too forcibly to the touch-judge in the match at Oldham and was reported in consequence. This little matter has increased Warrington's difficulty of putting a strong team in the field for the important match at Runcorn to-day. Points are at stake both in the Northern League and in the S'Outh• West Lmeashira Cup Competition.</p>
        <p>—ADvt. • Institute of Journalists at Warrington. The quarterly meeting of the Liverpool District of the Institute of Jonrnaliets was held last Saturday at the Town Hall. Warrington, by the courtesy of his Worship the Mayor (Alderman Bolton). Mr. A. E. -- - - Wigley, of Formby, presided in the absence of the 1 The best has been made of a bed joleandthe selected Chairman. Representatives were present from Liver- , fifteen if not very brilliant as an attacking eembina- pool, Werrington, Widnes. Runcorn and Southport.- . tion ought to be as linn as a re'tk on the defence. A report was submitted by the District Hon. I Isherwood is now the selo survivor of the regular Secretary (Mr. A. Vinden) reeler:tiny the annual three-quarters, anti the line is mede on of full hacke conference of the Institute, which was held at and half-backs. The team will be as follows : Hallam Bournemoooth. Regret was etpreesed that the cendi- date nominated by the Liverpool District far one full back ; Brooks, Isherwood, Hewitt and Knigilt three quarters ; Hoekenh ill and J. Davies. half backs. oF the five vacancies in the Vice-preeidener of the ouQk lmars, Preston, Thomas, Jolle7, iliitoa, Swift, Clot:, Institute was net suecessfal. With' regerd. to the -and-Harmer forward's. Oleo mere there will be a general proceedings of the conference the Secretary big responsibility on the front rank, bet if they repeat pointed out that amongst the numerous subjects dis- last week's for.n there »bald be a f sir prospect of crossed the question of copyright most closely affected obtaining paints at Runcorn. - the interests of the profession. Varier's. matters con- . --- cereing the Liverpool district were dealt with. . A.• The ll A" tesal hie a 0 enbirrttien in itch with deputation was appoinied with a view to arm- Runcorn " A " awl a rather scratch. dozea will take jug at an amicable settlement, if nessible, f o- a the fieltLyiz : Ceislit'en, full back ; Shaw Jordan,Liovd dispute between the Genn