 .1. Wondwer•l was in charge of the i • lantern, and there was a large attendance.</p>
        <p>Goals.</p>
        <p>P . W. L. D. For Aist Stockton Heath 2nd Latchford 2nd</p>
        <p>The following teams will represent Stockton Heath —First (away). F. G. Kartland, goal ; E, Pierpoint and L. Fairclough. backs : J. G. Hatton, H. Kirkconnel and E. R. Jones, halves; S. Baxter, R. Pierpoint, %V. H. Banks, W. Richardson, and T. Day, forwards. Bully- off. 2.45. Second (home) : A. Jones, goal Egerton Fairolough and?. B. Hawtin, backs : A. Hodgkinson, H. Smith and J. Houghton, halves ; L. Pierpoint, H. Owen, W. Howard, R. Dolan and W. Lionel, forwards. Bully-off, 2.45. Referee, N. W. Bellamy.</p>
        <p>Latchford were at Waterloo on Saturday and for the first time turned out at full strength. From the bully- off, Latchford showed a marked superiority over their opponents, Callon opened the scoring after about 15 minutes play. They afterwards continued to preas,their backs proving equal to almost all the attacks made on their goal, and eventually Knight secured, and beating several of the opposing players scored a capital goal after a praiseworthy run. This seemed to be emulated a few minutes after by the home centre forward, who beat all opposition to the visitors circle. Soon after the restart Jones met with an accident and was com- pelled to retire, so that Latchford played with only ten men. Neverthelesa they maintained the pressure, and repeatedly had their opponents in difnculties, only !to be repulsed before anything tangible could be recorded. The result although hardly representing the ' garne, was a win for Latchford by two goals to one.</p>
        <p>Latchford "A " played Sale "B " at Sale on Saturday last. Latchfordtaa rather a weak team, and in fact turned out one or two players short. Sale proved altogether too much for them and rushed five goals in during the first twenty minutes, Then Latch- ford seemed to recover, and held the home team in check, but could not the uselves score. No farther goals were added, and when time was called the result was Sale " B "5, Latchford " A "nil.</p>
        <p>The teams for to-day against Stockton Heath are : First eleven: Goal, W. Unsworth : fall backs, R. Hallows and F. Dixon; half-backs, W. Knight, J. B. Wilkinsou,and AlLlZathbone; forwards, W.EI. Spensley, E. F. Cliff, D. Knight. It. L. Jones and J. Callon. Second eleven : Goal, W. Bamber ; fall-backs. C. Hale n nil T. Young ; half-backs,W. B. Cook, G. FL Heald and D. Travis ; forwards, W. B. Smith, H. Warburton, A. Albinson. A. Allmder, and J. Wilkinson.</p>
