        <head>WARRINGTON TOWN COUNCIL. PURCPASE OF TRAMCAR COVERS</head>
        <p>WARRINGTON TOWN COUNCIL. PURCPASE OF TRAMCAR COVERS</p>
        <p>Alderman PRANCOMB in moving the confirmation of the minutes said the question of settlement was still in the hands of the Town Clerk. They asked the Leigh Corporation to pay the out of pocket expenses of the Committee. He hoped to be able to give further information at the meeting of the Council. Alderman EvANs seconded. Councillor WRIGHT said that at the last meeting of -- -- the Council it was reported that the supply of water in The final meeting for the year of the Warrington the Lovely-lane district would not be sufficient n the Town Council was held at the Town Hall on Tuesday event of a fire. He would like to know how it was that when there was present the Mayor (Alderman Bolton), the Engineer had been instructed to report upon the uestion when that had already been done. It would Aldermen A. Bennett, John Evans, R. W. Francomb, W. fl have been better had the Engineer been instructed to Pierpoint, J. Smethurst, and D, Tinnion, Councillors T. ,lderniau FRANCOMB explained that the Committee H. Ashcroft, T. Barton,W.Benson,W. Brough,T. Burton, lay the main. W. Clegg, J. G. Craik, James Evans, L. Ellison, T. J. A j. , Hulse, Dr. Joseph, J. Lord, J. Maginn, J. Pemberton, had three schemes before them, and the engineer had Sankey, J. Skelland, J. F. Smith, F. Stott, J. Wilkinson been instructed to report as to which scheme was the W.J.Wilson,T. Wright, Messrs J.L.Whittle(Town Clerk), best. THE PURCHASE OF TRAMCAR COVERS. .I.Fairhurst (Borough Treasurer), T. Longdin (Borough COUNCILLOR STOTT PROTESTS AGAINST Surveyor), J. Doss (Water Engineer), C. Madeley DELAY. (Librarian), W. S. Haddock (Gas Engineer), J. G. The Electricity and Tramways Committee recommen- Gornall (Medical (Meer), and J. M. Muriay (Director dad that tenders be invited for 4 additional tramcar of Education). PLANTING OF TREES. covers similar to the existing ones. Alderman SMETHURST moved and Councillor WILKLN- At a meeting of the Street Improvement and Lighting SON Committee several owners of property having expressed seconded the confirmation of the minutes. Councillor Srorr asked how it was that the purchase their desire to plant trees in certain streets of the of the additional covers had not been considered before. borough if the Corporation would look after the same, If the Committee had stipulated a short time in which it was resolved, that if the owners of property will pro- vide and plant suitable trees under the supervision of to complete delivery only one firm—the one at Birken- the head gardener, the Town Hall Parks and Baths head—could do the work. He would like to XDOW whether the advertisement had been published. Committee be recommended to look after and maintain The MA VOR : Not until it has been passed by the the same. • Alderman BENNETT in moving the confirmation of the Council. Alderman SMETHURST : The matter was an urgent minutes thought they should encourage the planting of one and the advertisement has been published ? trees and he hoped the Town Hall Parks and Baths Councillor s ...TOTT as a protest against the action of Committee would favourably consider the recom- the committee in advertising before obtaining the per- mendations. mission of the Council, moved that the minute be re- The minutes were approved. ferred back. He thought the permission of the Council COUNCILLOR LORD'S QUESTIONS, should be obtained before that had been done. He - Councillor LORD asked the Chairman of the Paving would like to know what the Committee had been doing and Sewerage Committee :—(1) What date was thei during the summer? They had had sufficient time to street called St. Barnabas-place paved? (2) To whom consider the question and the delay meant that the same was the contract let? (3) What is the reason why it firm would get the contract. He objected to ' the coin- has been taken up and re-paved ? (4) Why are the nsittee asking the Council for permission to advertise original setts being re-placed by others ? as H (51 the '' . and advertis