      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1905-11-04_WidnesExaminer_art0094" n="art0094">
        <head>ROUND TIM WORLD TILAVEL.</head>
        <p>ROUND TIM WORLD TILAVEL.</p>
        <p>Round the world re.iords have been of course revolutionised by the Canadian Pacific Railway with their fast steamers from Vancouver to Yokahama) and the Trans-Siberian Railway. This is no doubt the quickest route, and it has been done in 60 days. But to equal this record the element of chance in the matter of connec- tion at Vancouver, Yokohama, Nagasaki, Vladivostock and Moscow must be reckoned with. Then another important factor in the enterprise is the season chosen. For instance, though the fastest Atlantic passages are usually oade in the Autumn, the traveller ambitious of getting round the globe in the shortest possible time, should leave England M July or August before the Summer Service of the Canadian Pacific is taken off.</p>
      </div>
