        <p>COUNTY BOROUGH OF WARRINGTON.- EDUCATION COMMITTI3B. CLERK OF WORKS. The Sites and Buildinzs Cammittee iniite applications from competent persons for the post of (NARK OF WORKS to superintend the erection of the " Beamont " and " Bolton "Council schools, at a salary of £3 10s. a week. The succassful candidate must devote the whole of his time to the service of the Committee, and the lappointmeut will be subject to one week's notice on either side. Canvassing members of the Committee either personally or otherwise will be considered a disqualification. Applications, stating age and experience, accompanied by copies of not more than three testimonials of recent date, must beforwarded to the under-rigned by not later than noon cn Wednesday, the Bth November, 1905. J. MOORE MURRAY, Secretary and Director. Education Office, Sankey street, Warrington. 27th October, 1905.</p>
